KNOWNBUG gcc-only
main.c

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
A reduced-alignment typedef (int __attribute__((aligned(2)))) used as a struct
member should keep its alignment, as GCC and Clang do. CBMC currently
over-aligns it to the natural alignment because type-level and
member-declarator alignment attributes are indistinguishable in the front-end
IR. The _Static_asserts therefore fail today (CONVERSION ERROR); promote to
CORE once alignment provenance is tracked.
